    "narrative": "The core of the Austin Waves lineup today rests on the elite output of **Gunnar Henderson**, who secures our highest score of 81.87. With a favorable matchup against Bello and the wind blowing out, **Gunnar Henderson** gains significant equity from a rare BvP edge and a prime spot at #2 in the order. **Kyle Tucker** (74.46) and **Andy Pages** (67.47) follow closely, both capitalizing on a soft matchup against Ryne Nelson. **Andy Pages** is particularly well-positioned; his placement in the #2 hole maximizes his counting stat potential, while **Kyle Tucker** remains a perennial powerhouse whose daily efficiency remains insulated from the usual SP volatility, even against a middling arm like Nelson.\n\nThe decision-making process was highlighted by the tight margins at the bottom of the order. **Jackson Merrill** (51.97) holds the UTIL spot despite a difficult date with Zack Wheeler, but his defensive metrics\u2014specifically the opposing catcher\u2019s elite pop time\u2014dampen his SB floor, making him a marginal play. Conversely, **Miguel Andujar** was the most notable omission from the active roster. While his projected output of 34.66 was respectable, it fell well below our 40-point \"Zebras Floor\" required to preserve our daily game caps. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (55.25) and **Coby Mayo** (56.47) occupy high-variance roles today; while **Coby Mayo** faces a strong matchup context, his score is slightly suppressed by a unfavorable platoon split, whereas **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** must navigate a high-difficulty outing against Chris Sale, necessitating caution despite his pedigree. With **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** remaining sidelined on the IL, our roster depth is being tested, leaving us reliant on the high-upside surges from **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker** to offset the risks posed by elite arms like Sale and Wheeler.",
